                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "70bc57dd-0ae0-4c17-bf90-8a7a20173777",
                        "source_entry_id": "8500602c-75ab-3e25-bd2d-d357bdfa8f03",
                        "target_lang_word": "still life",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "still life",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1b336fac-5fd5-3820-bd51-ff09da4c4fdb",
                                        "entry_id": "b6c0c0ad-0005-38c6-b53c-d1bef0c46f19",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A work of art depicting an arrangement of inanimate objects."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0924a993-e3e9-349f-bf56-8370bf2f67d0",
                                        "entry_id": "b6c0c0ad-0005-38c6-b53c-d1bef0c46f19",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A pattern that does not change from one generation to the next."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f0ea2ad0-47d3-47ce-bddf-6682d2627bc4",
                                                "sense_id": "0924a993-e3e9-349f-bf56-8370bf2f67d0",
                                                "text": "I think you're talking about a configuration known as \"eater,\" a still life in 6-8 cells. If the glider hits the right spot, the eater will form a bridge and destroy the glider while undergoing little change before reverting."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "825e4e39-fdda-4917-8e7b-6653955b722f",
                                                "sense_id": "0924a993-e3e9-349f-bf56-8370bf2f67d0",
                                                "text": "Thus, a natural question, apparently proposed very early, was whether there exists a still life (i.e. period 1 oscillator) that reflects a glider."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5923891b-4e3a-4aa7-95ee-c0420695aa02",
                                                "sense_id": "0924a993-e3e9-349f-bf56-8370bf2f67d0",
                                                "text": "I haven't tested yet, but I expect hlife to win by a very large margin since the puffer train has lots of still life and blinkers to make Gosper's algorithm look good, and hlife's low-level implementation is quite good at handling the more random parts."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "5c691ad7-670c-4247-b832-282ef621715a",
                        "source_entry_id": "8500602c-75ab-3e25-bd2d-d357bdfa8f03",
